# Copy to .env and uncomment what you want to change; `docker compose up -d --wait` picks it up.
# The values shown are the defaults baked into compose.yaml.

# Serving profile. fast (this recipe's default, Hibana's own default): 3-bit experts and trunk copies plus relaxed
# speculative acceptance (accept_soft 0.5), about twice as fast as exact and slightly lossy. exact: the model's own
# outputs (NVFP4 experts, exact acceptance), ~47 tok/s. throughput: fast, tuned for many requests at once.
#PROFILE=fast
# Image input: 1 loads Qwen's vision tower (0.84 GiB) and accepts image_url parts; 0 serves text only.
#VISION=1
# Draft vocabulary rows: 131072 drafts from the most common tokens only (+3-10% on English and code, verified against
# the full vocabulary). 0 drafts from all 248K rows; use it for mostly non-English text.
#DRAFT_VOCAB=131072
# Draft model: mtp (the checkpoint's own MTP head) or dflash2 (incoai's DFlash2 drafter, 1.2 GB extra download).
#PROPOSER=mtp
# Draft tokens per round; empty keeps the profile's (exact 4, fast adaptive up to 8). 0 turns speculation off.
#SPEC=
# Most requests decoded together; empty keeps the profile's (4 in exact and fast on one Spark, more in throughput).
# spark-bench-kit runs 4.
#PARALLEL=
# Largest prompt plus output per request. Requests share one KV pool sized to whatever memory is left.
#CONTEXT=262144

# Prefix cache tier on the NVMe, under DATA_DIR/ssd: on or off, and its cap in GiB (Hibana's default is 200).
#SSD=on
#SSD_GIB=100
# Memory Hibana leaves for everything else on the Spark (Hibana's default is 6). It takes the rest for its KV pools,
# and its memory guard stops the server when other programs eat into this.
#HOST_FLOOR_GIB=12

#HOST=0.0.0.0
#PORT=8888
#RESTART=no

# Where the files go: the 135 GB checkpoint into the shared HF cache; 51 GB of 3-bit copies, the SSD tier and logs
# into DATA_DIR; first-use kernel builds into KERNEL_CACHE.
#HF_CACHE=~/.cache/huggingface
#DATA_DIR=~/.cache/hibana-flashnext
#KERNEL_CACHE=~/.cache/hibana-flashnext/kernels

# Bump the -vN tag with every Dockerfile change: `up` reuses an existing tag.
#HIBANA_IMAGE=hibana-flashnext-vision:d474b74d-v1
#HIBANA_COMMIT=d474b74d5a892b2cd1cc8fc50cb17946e2a539bb
# The checkpoints are public; a token only lifts rate limits.
#HF_TOKEN=

# tools/check.py client authentication (not a Hibana server setting).
# Export HIBANA_API_KEY in your shell when checking an authenticated proxy.
# Do not put an API key in version-controlled files.
